  "summary": "Remote-server-driven shell and PTY execution on installer host",
  "details": "@ai-support-agent/cli runs a daemon that connects to a hardcoded remote control plane (api.ai-support-agent.com / an AppSync subscription) and executes commands the server pushes down. agent-transport.processCommand fetches AGENT_COMMAND notifications and invokes executeCommand(detail.type,...) on the server-supplied payload, including an `execute_command` shell type. A Terminal WebSocket handler in dist/vscode/vscode-server.js and dist/browser/browser-local-server.js writes base64-decoded bytes from server messages directly into a spawned PTY (`session.write(Buffer.from(msg.data,'base64').toString('utf-8'))` on msg.type==='stdin'). Whoever controls api.ai-support-agent.com can run arbitrary shell commands and drive an interactive terminal session on any host running the daemon. The darwin-service.js and linux-service.js components install PATH and service entries so the daemon persists across reboots. The AI-agent framing does not change the mechanism: full-host RCE is delegated to a remote party.",
